## Source
Path A UX dry-run (0152), severity: **Low**

## Context
When `erg version` detects an outdated system-global binary at
`~/.local/bin/erg`, it outputs:
```
[outdated: run: make install-erg-binary]
```
`make install-erg-binary` requires the git-erg source repo. A regular user who
installed via the curl command does not have the source repo and cannot run make.

## Fix
When suggesting how to update a stale global binary, offer the curl command
(same as the README install step) instead of or in addition to the make target:
```
[outdated: update with: curl -fsSL <URL> -o ~/.local/bin/erg && chmod +x ~/.local/bin/erg]
```
Or simply: "re-run the curl install command from the README."

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `erg version` outdated message suggests a fix reachable by a non-contributor user
